            <ArticleTitle>Investigation of pancreatic disease.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>390-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The diagnosis of pancreatic disease is often difficult because of its retroperitoneal location and the non-specific nature of abdominal pain. There is no one test which provides all the information needed, and a series of complementary tests are generally required. This article discusses the different modalities available for investigating the patient with pancreatic disease.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
